#+TITLE: SAVEFORMAT + container/version default write format
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: feature
#+BRANCH: feat-saveformat-drawing-version

SAVEFORMAT (BricsCAD) + container/version default write format

== Context ==

The default drawing write format shipped in 2.2.83
(CLAUTOLISPDEFAULTDRAWINGFORMAT, issues/closed/cador-default-drawing-format.issue)
claimed "no vendor counterpart". That was wrong: BricsCAD has SAVEFORMAT, a
system variable (integer 1..30, default 1 = DWG 2018) that selects both the
container (DWG / DXF / Binary DXF) and the version. AutoCAD has NO such
sysvar — its default save format is an Options-dialog / registry preference.
pjb asked to check the references and honour the vendor mechanism, with the
default carrying container + version.

== Change (clautolisp 2.2.84) ==

- SAVEFORMAT (already a cador sysvar cell from the vendor catalogue) is now
  *functional*: under a BricsCAD dialect it selects the default write format.
  Full 1..30 decode -> (container . version) per the BricsCAD reference.

- CLAUTOLISPDEFAULTDRAWINGFORMAT extended to carry a version: the value is a
  container token (DXF / DXFB / DWG) optionally followed by a version label
  ("DWG-2013", "DXF2000", "DWG-R12"), case- and separator-insensitive.

- cador-default-drawing-format now returns (values CONTAINER VERSION),
  dialect-selected: BricsCAD dialect -> SAVEFORMAT; otherwise
  CLAUTOLISPDEFAULTDRAWINGFORMAT (the cross-dialect / AutoCAD-emulation knob).

- clautolisp.drawing:*default-drawing-version* (defvar nil) — the version
  companion of *default-drawing-format*, folded into write-drawing's version
  resolution (after explicit version and the drawing's own). cador's ActiveX
  SaveAs binds both specials.

The container axis is honoured for real (DXF-ascii / DXF-binary / DWG are
registered codecs). The version axis is recorded on the drawing and the DXF
$ACADVER header, but the DXF/DWG writers still emit a fixed version — a
STUB, tracked by issues/open/drawing-codec-version-output.issue.

Also corrected the harvested SAVEFORMAT inventory/spec note ("bit-coded" —
the vendor help says it is NOT bit-coded) and added its value table.

== Resolved ==

DONE — clautolisp 2.2.84 (2026-09-23). Tests: drawing suite 293/293
(*default-drawing-version* fallback), cador suite 1065/1065
(%parse-drawing-format-spec, %decode-saveformat, dialect source selection
under --bricscad, SaveAs records version). Docs: autolisp-spec §§ SAVEFORMAT
(+ *** clautolisp deviation) and CLAUTOLISPDEFAULTDRAWINGFORMAT (doc version
0.13.1 -> 0.13.2), clautolisp user manual, RELEASE_NOTES.org.
